	<div class="inner col col24 first last id33197a45-8b8f-479c-97d5-a85ab94ade46" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="33197a45-8b8f-479c-97d5-a85ab94ade46">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor327dcf31-59c5-4c72-9bbd-297f2e9c138b" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1">November 3, 2026, City Council District 1 Special Election</h2><p><br></p><p>Visit <a href="https://www.votedenton.gov/voter-information/voter-registration/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Denton County Elections</a> for information regarding voter registration.</p><p data-pasted="true"><strong>Early Voting:&nbsp;</strong>Monday, October 19 to Friday, October 30<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Election Day:&nbsp;</strong>Tuesday, November 3</p><p>For questions, contact the City Secretary&apos;s Office at (940) 349-8303 or email <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#a5e6ccd1dc8bf6c0c6d7c0d1c4d7dce5c6ccd1dccac3c1c0cbd1cacb8bc6cac8" id="isPasted"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="35765c414c1b66505647504154474c75565c414c5a5351505b415a5b1b565a58">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.&nbsp;</p><ul><li><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/12980" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.cityofdenton.com/DocumentCenter/View/12980" data-url-hash="5b02a4013006310843bed73f261adbc3cdec36fd4932db458bb044a79ee616bd" data-url-status="disabled">Calendar of Important Dates for 2026 General Election (PDF)</a></li></ul><h2 id="isPasted">Notice to Candidates:</h2><p>The City Secretary as Chief Election Official is responsible for providing potential local candidates and officeholders with the necessary forms for General Election purposes. Completed forms once filed with the City Secretary are public records and are open for inspection by any person through the Texas Public Information Act.</p><p>Please note, the City Secretary is NOT a legal adviser/ interpreter to candidates or officeholders for the completion of required forms. The responsibility for compliance with the Election Laws belongs solely with local candidates and officeholders.</p><p>Candidates and officeholders may direct questions about campaign finance law and candidacy to the Texas Ethics Commission at (512) 463-5800 or 1-800-325-8506 and the Texas Secretary of State at (512) 463-5650 or 1-800-252-8683. Information may also be accessed at <a aria-label="Link ethics.state.tx.us" href="https://www.ethics.state.tx.us/" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" title="https://www.ethics.state.tx.us/">ethics.state.tx.us</a> and <a aria-label="Link sos.state.tx.us" href="https://www.sos.state.tx.us/" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank" title="https://www.sos.state.tx.us/">sos.state.tx.us</a>.</p>
    </div>

